{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532557-v20-is-animalism-mind-control-emotion-manipulation-or-something-else","id":1532557,"title":"[V20] is Animalism Mind Control, Emotion Manipulation or something else","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-14T04:46:26-07:00","id":1532557,"title":"[V20] is Animalism Mind Control, Emotion Manipulation or something else","content":"WoD seems in general to distinguish between powers that influence your mind (for example Dominate and Dementation) and powers that influence your emotion (for example Presence), and there are often merits or other defensive features were it is said that they work against one type but not against the other.<br /> <br /> In which of the two categories does Animalsim fall or Animalsim is some third category?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T05:25:51-07:00","id":1532562,"title":"","content":"Animalism works on both. It is mind control and emotion control.<br /> <br /> The Mind Sphere of Mages also do both, so the difference between mind control in Domination and emotional control in Presence is a thing for Vampire, not universal of WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T10:35:20-07:00","id":1532658,"title":"","content":"WW didn't really define it in VtM. Even though other disciplines allow the simultaneous use of other disciplines dependent upon this definition. <br /> <br /> IMO, ST and table need to pick one and be consistent, mechanically. Stuff like possession allows the use of other disciplines while possessing a host, usually dependent on successes rolled. For Animalism I would endorse Animalism requiring fewer successes to use due to it being a bit less precise in its application. It doesn't require language or complex concepts to use. <br /> <br /> And I typically endorse Animalism4 being able to use the Animalism powers below it automatically - it just seems consistent to do so. Possessing an animal and trying to use Dominate? Well, seems fair you would need more successes in the activation roll and an animal that can mimic speech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T21:32:29-07:00","id":1532681,"title":"","content":"Neither. The beast is, in VTMverse, something distinct from emotions and mind. It might not make realistic sense, but it's the way the VTMverse works. Animals, being almost entirely the beast, are controllable by a discipline focused on controlling the beast. Other creatures, being more complex, are influenced in more specialized ways, such as Quell the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T23:58:42-07:00","id":1532684,"title":"","content":"Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> said, Animalism works through and on the Beast. That's important because, for example, Anmalism 3 cannot be used on a vampire who used the VDA20 Obfuscate 6 power in the core book (can't remember the powers' names today, sorry) because that power hides the vampire's Beast (among other things). <br /> <br /> Animalism: Beast control<br /> Dominate: hypnosis<br /> Presence: heighten the emotional response to the vampire's presence (the type of emotion depends on the power used)<br /> Obfuscate: mind numbing of a sort, so that perceptions of the vampire by others are altered within a certain radius<br /> Serpentis 1: an alluring and odd physical feature has a mystical enchanting effect (it's not stated to be mind or emotional control, nor Beast, so I put it in its own category, especially in VDA20 where I take the source of Serpentis to be different from Protean and from the other common disciplines)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T04:08:46-07:00","id":1532696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532557-v20-is-animalism-mind-control-emotion-manipulation-or-something-else?p=1532562#post1532562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mind Sphere of Mages also do both, so the difference between mind control in Domination and emotional control in Presence is a thing for Vampire, not universal of WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>But even in Mage you have for example different Merits to defend against both, Iron Will against Dominate and other Mind Controll effects und Judge\u2019s Wisdom against Presence and other types of emotinal manipulation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}